spec-5: expected-acceptance telemetry, sum_x min(p, q), from the MRv2 rejection sampler.

Research experiment for docs/research/deepinfer/spec-decode.md spec-5. NOT in patches/series.
Off unless SPEC5_TELEMETRY_DIR is set; with it unset rejection_sample gets accept_stats=None and
runs exactly the upstream kernels.

Why a server patch: the client never sees q. /v1/completions returns target logprobs for the
emitted tokens only, so the draft distribution, the rejected draft token and its target
probability are all invisible from outside, and sum_x min(p, q) needs all three.

With SPEC5_TELEMETRY_DIR=<dir>, after _rejection_kernel one extra Triton kernel (one program per
request) writes four rows per draft position i:
  overlap   sum_x min(p_i, q_i)                       (DeepInfer's accept_probs, fused_sample.py)
  survival  prod_{j<=i} min(1, p_j(d_j) / q_j(d_j))   E[accept at i | the drafts]
  drafts    1 per verified position
  accepted  1 if i < the accepted length              (the realised count, for the identity check)
p is the processed target distribution the sampler tests against, one-hot at the argmax for a
greedy request; q is softmax(draft_logits / T), or one-hot at the draft for a speculator that
passes no draft logits. Rows are summed over requests into a float64 [4, k] device tensor;
each verify step copies it non-blocking into pinned memory and the next step writes it to
<dir>/spec5-<pid>.json (cumulative since boot), so nothing waits on the GPU and the file lags
the device by one verify step. Greedy requests make survival == accepted exactly.

Cost when on: one launch per verify chunk plus a full-vocab pass per draft position only when
the speculator passes draft logits at T > 0; a ~200-byte D2H copy and a JSON write per step.
MRv2 only (v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode); the V1 runner's v1/sample/rejection_sampler.py is untouched.

Kind: experiment
Cut-against: ghcr.io/syv-ai/hyperqwen:latest site-packages/vllm (0.31.0 + patches/series)
Apply: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz 0 -d <site-packages/vllm> -i spec5-accept-telemetry.patch

